---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import models from '../data/models.json';
---
<Layout title="Pricing Sources & Calculation Method — AICost Matrix" description="See the exact scope, official sources, verification dates, billing buckets and limitations behind AICost estimates." canonical="https://aicost.apexcraftweb.com/methodology">
<div class="wrap narrow flow"><section><p class="eyebrow">Show the work</p><h1>Sources & methodology.</h1></section><section class="panel"><h2>Price coverage</h2><p>Three reference models from the direct Claude API. USD per million text tokens; global routing; standard service tier or asynchronous Message Batches. Prompts up to 100,000 tokens including cache reads and writes. Models are not ranked by speed or quality.</p>
{models.map(m=><details><summary>{m.name} · checked {m.verifiedAt}</summary><p>{m.sourceExcerpt}</p><p>Exact supported API ID: <code>{m.apiModel}</code></p><p><a href={m.sourceUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official price source ↗</a> · <a href={m.modelIdSource} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official model IDs ↗</a></p><p class="hint">Next review due {m.reviewAfter}. {m.reviewTrigger}</p></details>)}
<p>Provider documentation was checked on 2026-11-14. It did not supply a single effective date for these rows; this is a dated reference snapshot, not proof of a historical rate. Verification dates are maintained explicitly and never refreshed by a website build.</p><p>Review is manual, due weekly and when prices, schemas or model availability change. This site does not have a live price feed. If the review date is overdue, recheck the official source before using the estimate.</p></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>Formula and token semantics</h2><p><code>USD = Σ(tokens in bucket × rate per million ÷ 1,000,000)</code></p><p>The five buckets are uncached input, cache read, 5-minute cache write, 1-hour cache write, and output. On the supported direct Anthropic Messages API, <code>input_tokens</code> excludes cached reads and writes. It must not have the cache count subtracted a second time. The write total equals its 5m plus 1h breakdown.</p><p><a href="https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/prompt-caching" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official caching schema and pricing ↗</a></p><p>Batch is a 0.5× multiplier on these token categories. It can stack with caching for this specific provider/mode; no blanket discount is assumed for other providers. Billed thinking belongs in output. Tool fees are separate.</p><p>Daily calls = actions × calls per action + additional retry/fallback calls. Period fees = per-call fees × daily calls × selected days. Extra calls assume the same token profile. If actual calls differ, inspect their individual usage records instead.</p><p>Amounts display up to six decimal places; exports retain full calculation precision. Zero is displayed as $0.00, not “less than $0.01”. Volume scenarios change only call volume, not quality, hit rate or price.</p></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>What we do not infer</h2><ul><li>Unknown models, price tiers, billing fields and conflicting usage are blocked instead of matched to a similarly named model.</li><li>No streaming fragments, normalized LangChain usage or cloud marketplace records. The checker cannot prove pasted records came from a provider.</li><li>No implicit cache-write duration: nonzero writes require a 5m/1h breakdown. Duplicate message IDs block the full result.</li><li>No media, server tools, regional/fast premiums, tax, credits, private rates or other application expenses.</li><li>No cost per successful task without observed success labels, no automatic quality or reliability guarantees, and no bill certification.</li></ul><p>Price comparisons use an identical assumed token profile. Different models tokenize and solve tasks differently; test quality and actual billable usage on your own workload.</p></section>
<section class="panel"><h2>Older pages</h2><p>Earlier model and comparison URLs remain reachable with an unverified-data notice. Their old prices and performance claims are excluded from the active calculator. This does not imply the models are retired; it means we have not verified those entries for this version.</p></section></div></Layout>
